{
  "_about": "Plain names for the items in USDA's boxed beef report (LM_XB403) on the beef price board. Keys are USDA's description with runs of spaces collapsed to one, exactly as the Worker stores them. `name` is what pages show, `slug` is the page address (/beef-prices/<slug>/), so never change a slug once its page is live. `imps` is the Institutional Meat Purchase Specifications number and `fl` the fat limitation code USDA lists with it; `primal` groups the cut on the board; `also` is a common name the cut or its steaks are sold under, only where that is standard. An item missing here still works: snapshot.py makes a name and slug from USDA's text and prints a reminder to add it. `es` and `slug_es` are the Spanish name and page (/es/precios-de-carne-de-res/<slug_es>/); `also_es` is the common Spanish name.",

